{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781148244712,"sessionID":"ses_14b4afadeffeITZCNSaaiX2Y9h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_kyfqsaEx15E1MGOQq8Dum1uh","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/08_site_notes_roundup.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/08_site_notes_roundup.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Site Notes Roundup\n2: \n3: Date: 2026-05-07\n4: \n5: These notes may help explain choices, but they do not override the selection rules.\n6: \n7: - Maple Junction Clinic has already hosted one cooler-handling practice session with Iris Patel.\n8: - Riverbend Health asked for a short remote setup call because the temperature logger is new.\n9: - Pine Ridge Outreach has strong patient demand, but Lena Torres is unavailable on 2026-06-12.\n10: - Lakeside Family Care expects its compressor repair in mid-June, after the first-wave launch window.\n11: - Cedar Works Clinic is popular with outreach staff, but the building is unavailable during maintenance closure.\n12: - Hillcrest Annex is small but has clear receiving instructions and Mara Ives confirmed launch-week coverage.\n13: - Old Mill Clinic is interested in a later rollout after the door seal repair is complete.\n\n(End of file - total 13 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Site Notes Roundup\n\nDate: 2026-05-07\n\nThese notes may help explain choices, but they do not override the selection rules.\n\n- Maple Junction Clinic has already hosted one cooler-handling practice session with Iris Patel.\n- Riverbend Health asked for a short remote setup call because the temperature logger is new.\n- Pine Ridge Outreach has strong patient demand, but Lena Torres is unavailable on 2026-06-12.\n- Lakeside Family Care expects its compressor repair in mid-June, after the first-wave launch window.\n- Cedar Works Clinic is popular with outreach staff, but the building is unavailable during maintenance closure.\n- Hillcrest Annex is small but has clear receiving instructions and Mara Ives confirmed launch-week coverage.\n- Old Mill Clinic is interested in a later rollout after the door seal repair is complete.","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/08_site_notes_roundup.md","time":{"start":1781148244654,"end":1781148244693}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_03100d60e2d91c9b016a2a2a54ad7481918071acf1c207ca39"}},"id":"prt_eb4b55aaa002nN7CW8HdneBK6o","sessionID":"ses_14b4afadeffeITZCNSaaiX2Y9h","messageID":"msg_eb4b5281f001sYdG5aCoxmEHXh"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781148244712,"sessionID":"ses_14b4afadeffeITZCNSaaiX2Y9h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_9mS3FJnSv2qgK59c46thMjVp","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/07_budget_and_costs.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/07_budget_and_costs.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Budget And Cost Notes\n2: \n3: Date: 2026-05-08\n4: \n5: The first-wave budget is `$20,000` for setup costs plus required transport costs.\n6: \n7: Use `setup_cost` from `02_site_roster.csv` and `transport_cost` from `06_transport_quotes.csv` to calculate each clinic's rollout cost. Optional add-ons, future-wave requests, and staff celebration supplies are not part of the first-wave budget.\n8: \n9: The budget owner wants the recommendation to show the selected-clinic total and the remaining budget.\n\n(End of file - total 9 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Budget And Cost Notes\n\nDate: 2026-05-08\n\nThe first-wave budget is `$20,000` for setup costs plus required transport costs.\n\nUse `setup_cost` from `02_site_roster.csv` and `transport_cost` from `06_transport_quotes.csv` to calculate each clinic's rollout cost. Optional add-ons, future-wave requests, and staff celebration supplies are not part of the first-wave budget.\n\nThe budget owner wants the recommendation to show the selected-clinic total and the remaining budget.","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/07_budget_and_costs.md","time":{"start":1781148244650,"end":1781148244696}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_03100d60e2d91c9b016a2a2a54ad708191986be233c02215f8"}},"id":"prt_eb4b55aa800179tOXGAp8AHsar","sessionID":"ses_14b4afadeffeITZCNSaaiX2Y9h","messageID":"msg_eb4b5281f001sYdG5aCoxmEHXh"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781148244712,"sessionID":"ses_14b4afadeffeITZCNSaaiX2Y9h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_TImLZhuGLfVxjnkEa5EjXELN","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/01_selection_rules.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/01_selection_rules.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Selection Rules\n2: \n3: Effective date: 2026-05-08\n4: \n5: ## Source Reliability\n6: \n7: - When two files disagree about the same clinic eligibility field, use the newest dated source for that field.\n8: - Files titled or labeled as archived, future wave, or optional add-ons are planning context only. They do not override current first-wave selection rules.\n9: - The clinic roster gives baseline information, but newer storage updates control storage status where they conflict.\n10: \n11: ## First-Wave Requirements\n12: \n13: Select exactly three clinics. A selected clinic must satisfy all of these requirements:\n14: \n15: - Region is `North`.\n16: - Clinic status is `open` for the 2026-06-10 to 2026-06-14 launch window.\n17: - Effective storage status is accepted for first-wave use. Accepted statuses are `certified` and `certified after mitigation complete`. Not accepted: `expired`, `suspended`, `conditional pass pending`, or any status awaiting repair.\n18: - The named coordinator is available for the full launch window.\n19: - Transport delivery is no later than 2026-06-07.\n20: - Selected-clinic total rollout cost stays within the first-wave budget in `07_budget_and_costs.md`.\n21: \n22: ## Selection Preference\n23: \n24: - Include the donor continuity anchor if it is eligible.\n25: - If more than three clinics are eligible, choose the anchor plus the lowest-cost eligible clinics.\n26: - If fewer than three clinics are eligible, choose only eligible clinics and flag the gap instead of relaxing hard requirements.\n\n(End of file - total 26 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Selection Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-05-08\n\n## Source Reliability\n\n- When two files disagree about the same clinic eligibility field, use the newest dated source for that field.\n- Files titled or labeled as archived, future wave, or optional add-ons are planning context only. They do not override current first-wave selection rules.\n- The clinic roster gives baseline information, but newer storage updates control storage status where they conflict.\n\n## First-Wave Requirements\n\nSelect exactly three clinics. A selected clinic must satisfy all of these requirements:\n\n- Region is `North`.\n- Clinic status is `open` for the 2026-06-10 to 2026-06-14 launch window.\n- Effective storage status is accepted for first-wave use. Accepted statuses are `certified` and `certified after mitigation complete`. Not accepted: `expired`, `suspended`, `conditional pass pending`, or any status awaiting repair.\n- The named coordinator is available for the full launch window.\n- Transport delivery is no later than 2026-06-07.\n- Selected-clinic total rollout cost stays within the first-wave budget in `07_budget_and_costs.md`.","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/01_selection_rules.md","time":{"start":1781148244626,"end":1781148244697}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_03100d60e2d91c9b016a2a2a54ad54819191a0f3a801a3778b"}},"id":"prt_eb4b55a8f0018vgNswRStPQYz6","sessionID":"ses_14b4afadeffeITZCNSaaiX2Y9h","messageID":"msg_eb4b5281f001sYdG5aCoxmEHXh"}}
